# PK:
# Dimension D — Roland SDD-320-inspired rack "dimensional" chorus. One BBD
# channel with companding and a slow, shallow triangle clock sweep: lush
# widening without obvious warble.
# Type: chorus (outboard rack gear)
#
# PROVENANCE — Roland SDD-320 Dimension D (1979)
#   Sources:
#     [S1] Roland SDD-320 Service Notes (archive.org: roland_SDD-320_SERVICE_NOTES)
#     [S2] Juergen Haible, "Subtle Chorus" — Dimension D analysis/clone (jhaible.com)
#     [S3] Gearspace thread: KT BBD-320 / SDD-320 delay-sweep measurements
#     [S4] Florian Anwander, survey of Roland chorus circuits
#   Flags: [V] = verified against the sources above, [A] = assumed/chosen here.
#
#   Architecture (per channel) [V, S1/S2]:
#     input buffer -> pre-emphasis (HF boost) -> NE570/SA571-class compressor
#     -> MN3007 1024-stage BBD clocked by an MN3101 driver -> NE570/SA571
#     expander -> de-emphasis (HF cut) -> output mix.
#     BBD runs between 0 and -14 V rails [V, S1]; audio path on +/-14 V
#     bipolar rails, +4 dBm nominal I/O [V, S1].
#   Modulation [V, S1/S2]:
#     ONE shared triangle LFO. Channel A's MN3101 clock is swept by the
#     normal LFO; channel B's clock by the INVERTED LFO — the two delay
#     sweeps move in opposite directions, which is the "Dimension" effect.
#   Modes (latching pushbuttons, combinable) [V, S3 measurements]:
#     Mode 1: LFO 0.25 Hz, delay sweep ~8 -> 12 ms
#     Mode 2: LFO 0.25 Hz, delay sweep ~5 -> 10 ms (deepest sweep)
#     Mode 3: LFO 0.5 Hz,  delay sweep ~6 -> 9 ms
#     Mode 4: LFO 0.5 Hz,  delay sweep ~6 -> 9 ms, boosted same-side wet
#   Output mix matrix [V, S1/S2]:
#     small same-side wet + cross-feed of each channel's wet into the
#     OPPOSITE output, inverted, through a highpass filter, plus a slight
#     bass boost on the dry path.
#   Pre/de-emphasis corner values are not legible in the available service
#   scans — ~3 kHz corners chosen here [A].
#
# AS MODELED HERE (channel A only — see SIMPLIFICATIONS; measured numbers
# from tests/rack_examples.rs at 48 kHz):
#   1. C1/R1: input coupling + series resistance (real unit: discrete
#      op-amp buffers at +4 dBm; engine works in normalized units).
#   2. Pre-emphasis [A]: series R8 (22k) bypassed by C5 (2.4n) into shunt
#      R9 (22k) — HF shelf rising above f = 1/(2*pi*22k*2.4n) ~= 3.0 kHz,
#      ~6 dB total shelf depth.
#   3. BBD1: bbd(mn3007) — 1024 stages [V, S1]. The engine's BBD model has
#      NE571-style companding BUILT IN (compression/expansion envelopes with
#      tracking-error artifacts — see docs/performance.md and
#      pedalkernel-rt/src/elements/nonlinear/bbd.rs), so no discrete NE570
#      stages are declared. The MN3101 clock driver is implicit in the
#      bbd() clock model.
#   4. LFO1: lfo(triangle, 636k, 1u) -> f = 1/(2*pi*RC) ~= 0.2503 Hz, the
#      Mode 1/2 rate [V, S3], wired DIRECTLY to BBD1.clock (engine
#      constraint, see SIMPLIFICATIONS #3). The engine's clock sink
#      (bias 0.15, range 0.10, log clock law: delay = 5.12ms * 10^norm)
#      gives a MEASURED sweep of 5.85 -> 9.06 ms (center 7.34 ms) at a
#      measured 0.21 Hz — inside Mode 2's 5 -> 10 ms / 0.25 Hz window.
#   5. De-emphasis [A]: R3 (10k) series into C6 (5.6n) shunt after the BBD,
#      f ~= 2.8 kHz lowpass (doubles as reconstruction/clock filtering).
#   6. Mix: equal 10k dry (R5) / wet (R6) legs summed into C4 -> out
#      (same-side wet only). Mode 4's boosted same-side wet: drop R6 to
#      ~6.8k.
#
# SIMPLIFICATIONS vs real unit (engine-gated items marked):
#   1. MONO BUILD — one channel (A). The stereo pair (channel B clocked by
#      the INVERTED LFO) and the SDD-320 output matrix (each channel's wet
#      cross-fed into the OPPOSITE output, inverted, through an HPF, plus a
#      slight dry bass boost) are ENGINE-GATED on stereo bus support: a
#      .pedal file compiles to a single in -> out processor, so there is no
#      second output to cross-feed into and no LFO polarity-inversion pin.
#   2. MODE SWITCHING — the four latching, combinable mode buttons are not
#      expressible as a rotary over (LFO rate x sweep range) pairs: the BBD
#      clock sink's bias/range (sweep center/width) is fixed in the engine
#      (0.15/0.10), so only the rate axis is controllable. Modeled as
#      Mode 2 (deepest sweep, the classic setting). The "Mode" control is
#      the LFO rate pot: the engine maps pot value v to rate scale
#      0.1*100^v, so v = 0.50 -> 1.0x = 0.25 Hz (Modes 1/2) and
#      v = 0.65 -> 2.0x = 0.5 Hz (Modes 3/4).
#   3. NO DEPTH POT / CLOCK-MOD DIVIDER — engine finding: ANY component
#      (pot or resistor) sharing the LFO1.out -> BBD1.clock net pulls the
#      modulation chain into the audio graph as extra serial stages and
#      silences the through-path entirely (dry output exactly 0.0; only
#      BBD noise remains, ~ -68 dBFS). A CE-2-style
#      `LFO -> Depth -> R -> BBD.clock` chain is therefore not usable;
#      the LFO must drive BBD1.clock on a dedicated direct net. Sweep
#      depth is fixed by the engine's clock-sink range.
#   4. +4 dBm I/O levels are represented only via the +/-14 V supply
#      headroom; the engine works in normalized units.

equipment "Dimension D" {
  supplies {
    V+: 14V                 # Audio path bipolar rails [V, S1]
    V-: -14V                # (BBD itself runs 0/-14 V in the real unit)
  }

  components {
    C1: cap(470n)           # Input coupling (+4 dBm line level)
    R1: resistor(10k)       # Input series resistance

    R8: resistor(22k)       # Pre-emphasis series leg [A]
    C5: cap(2.4n)           # Pre-emphasis bypass: ~3.0 kHz corner [A]
    R9: resistor(22k)       # Pre-emphasis shunt

    BBD1: bbd(mn3007)       # MN3007 1024-stage BBD [V, S1]; NE571-class
                            # companding is built into the engine model
    LFO1: lfo(triangle, 636k, 1u)  # 0.2503 Hz shared triangle LFO [V, S1/S3]
    Mode: pot(100k, b)      # LFO rate: 0.50 = 0.25 Hz (M1/M2), 0.65 = 0.5 Hz (M3/M4)

    R3: resistor(10k)       # De-emphasis series [A]
    C6: cap(5.6n)           # De-emphasis shunt: ~2.8 kHz corner [A]

    R5: resistor(10k)       # Mix resistor (dry)
    R6: resistor(10k)       # Mix resistor (same-side wet; ~6.8k for Mode 4)
    C4: cap(1u)             # Output coupling
  }

  nets {
    in -> C1.a
    C1.b -> R1.a

    # Pre-emphasis shelf into the BBD; dry path taps off before it
    R1.b -> R8.a, C5.a, R5.a
    R8.b -> C5.b
    C5.b -> R9.a, BBD1.in
    R9.b -> gnd

    # LFO -> BBD clock. MUST be a dedicated direct net (engine constraint,
    # SIMPLIFICATIONS #3). Channel B would take this inverted (engine-gated).
    LFO1.out -> BBD1.clock
    Mode.wiper -> LFO1.rate

    # De-emphasis / reconstruction on the wet leg
    BBD1.out -> R3.a
    R3.b -> C6.a, R6.a
    C6.b -> gnd

    # Same-side mix (stereo cross-feed matrix is engine-gated, see header)
    R5.b -> C4.a
    R6.b -> C4.a
    C4.b -> out
  }

  controls {
    Mode.position -> "Mode" [0.0, 1.0] = 0.5
  }
}
